From: AshesTom <258768419+AshesTom@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] kernelbase: Windows 7's shell32 sees the shell as explorer.exe

Purpose: fill the Start menu's list of programs used most (its left column
was empty, except for pinned programs).

Windows behavior: Windows 7's shell32 keeps the Start menu's cache of
programs (StartPage2's ProgramsCache, from which the list of the programs
used most is made with UserAssist) only in a process whose file is
EXPLORER.EXE (GetModuleFileNameW, then a comparison of the name).

Wine before: the Windows 7 shell runs as w7-explorer.exe (patch 0125 and
the prefix keep its DLLs apart by that name), so the cache was never filled
and no program used appeared, however often launched.

Change: in the Windows 7 shell session, GetModuleFileNameW(NULL) called from
shell32 in w7-explorer.exe returns the same path with the name
explorer.exe. Other callers, and other modules, still get w7-explorer.exe.

Evidence: headless Windows 7 session: after launching KCalc and Gwenview from
All Programs, the Start menu lists them below the pinned programs (before:
nothing, also after a restart of the session).

Scope: the external shell, WIN4WINE_SHELL=win7, the process w7-explorer.exe.
---
 dlls/kernelbase/loader.c |   22 ++++++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 22 insertions(+)

diff --git a/dlls/kernelbase/loader.c b/dlls/kernelbase/loader.c
--- a/dlls/kernelbase/loader.c
+++ b/dlls/kernelbase/loader.c
@@ -292,6 +292,26 @@
 }
 
 
+/* win4wine: Windows 7's shell32 keeps the Start menu's cache of programs
+ * (its list of the programs used most) only in EXPLORER.EXE, and the Windows 7
+ * shell runs as w7-explorer.exe. Asked by shell32, the shell's own file name
+ * is explorer.exe, in the same folder. */
+static void win7_shell_file_name( LPWSTR filename, ULONG *len, void *caller )
+{
+    static const WCHAR shell[] = L"\\w7-explorer.exe";
+    const ULONG shell_len = ARRAY_SIZE(shell) - 1, alias_len = ARRAY_SIZE(L"\\explorer.exe") - 1;
+    HMODULE shell32;
+    void *base;
+
+    if (*len < shell_len || wcsnicmp( filename + *len - shell_len, shell, shell_len )) return;
+    if (win4wine_shell() != WIN4WINE_SHELL_WIN7) return;
+    if (!(shell32 = GetModuleHandleW( L"shell32.dll" )) || !RtlPcToFileHeader( caller, &base ) ||
+        base != (void *)shell32)
+        return;
+    memcpy( filename + *len - shell_len, L"\\explorer.exe", (alias_len + 1) * sizeof(WCHAR) );
+    *len -= shell_len - alias_len;
+}
+
 /***********************************************************************
  *	GetModuleFileNameW   (kernelbase.@)
  */
@@ -314,6 +334,8 @@
     name.MaximumLength = min( size, UNICODE_STRING_MAX_CHARS ) * sizeof(WCHAR);
     status = LdrGetDllFullName( module, &name );
     if (!status || status == STATUS_BUFFER_TOO_SMALL) len = name.Length / sizeof(WCHAR);
+    if (!module && !status && win4wine_external_shell())
+        win7_shell_file_name( filename, &len, __builtin_return_address(0) );
     SetLastError( RtlNtStatusToDosError( status ));
 done:
     TRACE( "%s\n", debugstr_wn(filename, len) );
